# tend root for locate run `{{run_id}}` — preset `{{preset}}`

Generated by `cf plan-locate`. Do not hand-edit: regenerate instead, so `run.yaml` keeps
recording the prompt shas that were actually used.

| | |
|---|---|
| entrypoint | `{{entrypoint}}` |
| gate (out of tree) | `{{gate_dir}}/{{gate_script}} --gate-config {{gate_dir}}/gate.json` |
| task manifests | `{{gate_dir}}/tasks/<task-id>.json` |
| sourceset | `{{sourceset_pin}}` |
| universe | `{{universe_pin}}` |
| bridge | `{{bridge}}` |
| model | `{{model}}` |
| tasks | {{task_count}} |
| concurrency | {{max_workers}} workers / {{max_reviewers}} reviewers |

`gate/` holds the locate gate, its task manifests, the head-text helper `locate_text.py`, the
passage-id tool, the two read-only corpus tools and `vendor/` with both vendored packages; it is
outside every worktree, and a worker can run its tools but not change them. Each task writes
`findings/<task-id>/<source-id>.json` for the sources its manifest names, and nothing else.

The worker reads `CF_EXTRA_TOOLS` (the corpus tools' allowlist entries), `CF_TASK_MANIFESTS`,
`CF_ATTEMPT_CAP` and `CF_FINDINGS_GLOB` from its wrapper in `bin/`. Start with a **1/1 smoke
test** and watch one task through worker → gate → reviewer → merge before raising the limits:

```bash
uv run tend-control limits --root {{tend_root}} --workers 1 --reviewers 1
uv run tend run --root {{tend_root}} --log-level INFO
# ... one task all the way through ...
uv run tend-control limits --root {{tend_root}} --workers {{max_workers}} --reviewers {{max_reviewers}}
```

Set a budget ceiling before raising concurrency: a locate run is not sent anywhere without one.
